\subsection{Determinants of the adult comparison}\label{sec:res-adult}

With sensor noise alone, Neuromag led both OPM arrays: the median paired ratio over the << F.g2_n_targets >> targets was << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_int_ratio >> for the dense array and << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_int_ratio >> for the site-matched array (Fig.~\ref{fig:conditions}). Brain noise changed the comparison. With the room field included, brain noise made up << F.g2_noise_share_dense_brain_pct >> of a dense-array OPM channel's in-band variance and << F.g2_noise_share_squid_mag_brain_pct >> of a Neuromag magnetometer's, whose room-field share was << F.g2_noise_share_squid_mag_room_pct >>. With sensor plus brain noise, the dense array's ratio was << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >> ($D$ = << F.wr_adult_dense_ib_db >>~dB), and the OPM was ahead at << F.wr_g2_ahead_n >> of the << F.g2_n_targets >> targets. The site-matched array's ratio was << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci >> ($D$ = << F.wr_adult_matched_ib_db >>~dB), with no established advantage.

Which Neuromag channels and which SNR measure entered the comparison changed the number. Against the << F.g2_squid_grad_channels >> gradiometers alone, the ratios were << F.g2_dense_vs_grad_ib_ratio >> (dense) and << F.g2_matched_vs_grad_ib_ratio >> (site-matched), and against the << F.g2_squid_sites >> magnetometers << F.g2_dense_vs_mag_ib_ratio >> and << F.g2_matched_vs_mag_ib_ratio >>. By peak-channel SNR, the closest analogue of the sensor-level SNRs of clinical studies (Section~S1), the dense array was ahead of the magnetometers (<< F.g2_peak_dense_vs_mag_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_peak_dense_vs_mag_ib_ci >>) but behind the best of all << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels (<< F.g2_peak_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_peak_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >>). By mean-power SNR, the dense array's advantage was small (<< F.g2_meanpow_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >>) and the site-matched array's was << F.g2_meanpow_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_meanpow_matched_vs_combined_ib_ci >>.

The OPM noise floor could remove or reverse the advantage. From << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_min >> to << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz, the dense array's ratio fell from << F.g2_sens_asd7ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> to << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >>, and the site-matched array's from << F.g2_sens_asd7ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> to << F.g2_sens_asd30ft_matched_vs_combined_ib_ratio >>. The break-even white noise was << F.rev_ns_breakeven_dense_vs_combined_ib_asd >> << F.rev_ns_breakeven_dense_vs_combined_ib_asd_ci >>~fT/√Hz for the dense array and << F.rev_ns_breakeven_matched_vs_combined_ib_asd >> << F.rev_ns_breakeven_matched_vs_combined_ib_asd_ci >>~fT/√Hz for the site-matched array (Fig.~\ref{fig:noise}D).

