The omissions we could test moved the advantage little at << F.g2_opm_asd_primary >>~fT/√Hz (Fig.~\ref{fig:noise}C; Table~S4). The cortex << F.rev_ns_joint_floor_mm >>--<< F.rev_ns_near_rule_mm >>~mm from the inner skull gave << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_bg_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> when added as background and << F.rev_ns_near_primary_f2mm_targets_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> when added as targets. A 1/$f$ component with a << F.rev_ns_joint_corner_hz >>-Hz corner gave << F.rev_ns_col_bv_asd15ft_c10hz_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> under the primary detector and << F.rev_ns_col_fr_asd15ft_c10hz_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> under one that also whitens across frequency, and cardiac and ocular sources changed the dense ratio by << F.rev_ns_ff_dense_vs_combined_ib_change_pct_range >>. The joint run of near-skull background and the << F.rev_ns_joint_corner_hz >>-Hz corner, with frequency whitening (Fig.~\ref{fig:noise}D, dashed), gave << F.rev_ns_joint_nofar_asd15ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.rev_ns_joint_nofar_asd15ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_primary >>, << F.rev_ns_joint_nofar_asd20ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio_3dp >> << F.rev_ns_joint_nofar_asd20ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci_3dp >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_20 >> and << F.rev_ns_joint_nofar_asd30ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz. Under the joint run, the advantage was thus established up to << F.g2_opm_asd_primary >> but not at << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_20 >>~fT/√Hz, against up to << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_20 >> (<< F.g2_sens_asd20ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ratio >> << F.g2_sens_asd20ft_dense_vs_combined_ib_ci >>) but not << F.g2_opm_asd_sweep_max >>~fT/√Hz under the primary model.

